# Immaterial.ask -- Ableton Live theme XML, converted by tools/themes/ask_to_theme.py
# IMMATERIAL_MOD: Immaterial with ONE ROLE CHANGED, THE ACCENT
# (ViewCheckControlEnabledOn) D6B762 in place of Immaterial's pink FF91C3
# (architect 2026-11-05, session 56, his pick m1 of the session's mocks: a
# separate theme, `immaterial` unchanged -- "lowest overhead, most honest,
# and least churn if reversed"; THE SHADE 2026-11-06, session 62, his pick
# x2, "my eye was biased by the small diffs"; the `_mod` suffix marks a
# theme modified by hand or by rule, session 86, 2026-11-07).
#
# THE RECIPE: Immaterial's own SearchIndication ECCA6D, its muted gold,
# SHADED IN OKLCH (Bjorn Ottosson's matrices): its lightness set to L 78.8,
# the lightness of the FF91C3 it replaces, so the accent sits over the ground
# at the ~55 L Live gives Default and Immaterial alike; its hue kept (89.7);
# its chroma scaled by 78.8 / its own L; each linear channel clipped to
# [0, 1], sRGB-encoded, rounded half to even and clamped: D6B762. The plain
# ECCA6D read "too bright" (+61 L over the ground). The accent is the
# markers' chip and a lit key's face, and the lit press fill and the
# lit-but-inert face derive from it; every other role is Immaterial's. The
# shade was the app's own rule over Immaterial.ask 2026-11-05 .. 11-11
# (src/gui/theme_ask.cpp,
# git history); since 2026-11-11, session 110, it is this file's one baked
# word.
# ScrollbarInnerTrack and ClipBorder added by hand from Immaterial.ask (architect 2026-11-17, session 140)
# WindowBackground, TitleForeground and SidebarForeground, our own roles (not Live's), added by hand: WindowBackground this file's SurfaceArea, TitleForeground and SidebarForeground its ControlForeground, so nothing here changes look (architect 2026-11-19, send Z)
# TooltipBackground, CardBackground and CardStandingBackground, our own fills (not Live's), added by hand: TooltipBackground this file's SurfaceBackground, CardBackground and CardStandingBackground its Alert, opaque, so nothing here changes look (send AA's stage D1, 2026-11-19)
# ScaleTrough, our own role (not Live's), added by hand: this file's ScrollbarInnerTrack, so nothing here changes look (send AA's stage D2, 2026-11-19)
# ScaleSliderBorder, our own role (not Live's), added by hand: this file's ClipBorder, so nothing here changes look (send AA's stage D3, 2026-11-19)
# ButtonHoverBackground and ScrollbarSliderHover, our own roles (not Live's), added by hand: ButtonHoverBackground this file's SurfaceBackground, ScrollbarSliderHover its ScrollbarInnerHandle, so no hover shows here (send CC, 2026-11-20)
# PlayheadLine, HoverLine, CueHover, PlayheadHover, CueDisabledHover and CueDisabledLabelHover, our own roles (not Live's), added as tools/themes/ask_to_theme.py writes them: PlayheadLine white half way to this file's RangeDefault (the playhead's line as the derivation drew it), HoverLine its ScrollbarInnerHandle, CueHover its ViewCheckControlEnabledOn, PlayheadHover its RangeDefault, CueDisabledHover its BackgroundClip, CueDisabledLabelHover its TextDisabled, so the playhead's line keeps its look and no marker or playhead hover shows here (architect 2026-11-21, send FF)
